// DECEMBER 10 — THE WISH
// Starts from Dec10_Dorm_Return. Anin is alone; this is one uninterrupted cutscene.
// UI SETUP: Add CutsceneCanvas to Dorm and assign the four imported character highlights
// in CutsceneView's Pictures list. Keep StorySplashOverlay for the calendar beats.
// Assign calendar-1 and calendar-2 to that overlay.
// ANIMATION TODO: Climb into bed and eyes-open/close sleep art. The fear flinch uses the existing sprite.
// CAMERA TODO: Close in on the circled calendar after Anin shuts her eyes.
// The calendar reset now opens on the first playable repeat of December 10.

title: Dec10_Wish_FlashbackState
tags: setup testing
---
// Never start this node. The two flags route the Classroom memory back to Dorm.
<<declare $dec10_wish_flashback = false>>
<<declare $dec10_wish_resume = false>>
===

title: Dec10_Wish_Dorm
tags: december10 dorm night wish testing
---
// Match the December 9 Dorm entrance: reveal the empty room, then open the door
// and let Anin walk in. Her current stopping point remains X 5.48.
// Hide before <<cinematic_start>>: it waits for the bars to slide in, and Anin would
// show at the door spawn during that wait, then vanish (the glitch on arrival).
<<hide "Kirana">>
<<hide "Anin">>
<<cinematic_start>>
<<delay 0.5>>
<<open_door "Dorm">>
<<show "Anin">>
<<start_character_move "Anin" 5.48 3 "walk" 0>>
<<wait_for_character_moves>>
<<face_character "Anin" "right">>
<<close_door "Dorm">>
Anin: These last few days at school have been so damn fun.
Anin: Seeing my friends without having to study for once.
Anin: Just hanging out, talking, making one last batch of memories together.
Anin: It feels like i knew them since forever.
<<face_character "Anin" "right">>
<<delay 1>>

// Full-screen picture cutscene: text appears beneath each character image, as in Scene1-NEW.
<<cinematic_end>>
<<cutscene_image "highlight-kirana">>
Kirana.
My best friend and my roommate.
We've shared a room since our first year here.
Back then, we weren't even that close. We fought about something almost every day.
Like when my alarm went off, I'd snooze it and go right back to sleep. Again and again.
She said I had no discipline. Can you believe her?
That's our group leader for you. Always looking out for us.
Her parents have already planned her whole life after school. She's pretty much set.

<<cutscene_image "highlight-lila">>
Lila. The loud one.
When she's not around, you can feel how quiet everything gets.
Loud and dumb, too.
She once fell for a delivery scam because someone said her package had arrived four hours after she ordered it.
Girl, you ordered from another island. Four hours? At least be suspicious.
She's the type to believe any gossip she hears.
But then again, even someone as dumb as her knows where she's headed.
Journalism. With her camera skills and how she can make friends with anyone, she's basically set for life.

<<cutscene_image "highlight-dira">>
Dira.
The only sane one in our group.
She's honestly perfect. Smart, calm, kind.
Sometimes I feel bad that she hangs out with disasters like us.
Maybe that's why our group has lasted, though. We're all so different.
And like the others, she knows where she's going. Probably overprepared, honestly.

<<cutscene_image "highlight-fal">>
Fal.
Of all the boys I've met at this school, he seems... different.
It's like we understand each other really well.
Whenever one of us needs something, the other one is there.
He's pretty amazing, isn't he?
But lately he's seemed down. I wonder what happened.
<<cutscene_end>>

// Anin walks to the far-left window. Keep the normal dialogue bubble over her.
<<cinematic_start>>
<<close_dialogue_bubble>>
<<move_character "Anin" -8.98748 3 "walk">>
Anin: How do they all know what they want to do after school?
Anin: All I wanted was to keep enjoying high school forever.
Anin: And look where that got me. I still have no clue what I want to be. Graduation's tomorrow. Shoot, I'm too late.
Anin: I'm... scared.
// Anin takes one backward step, pauses, then shudders as the next line appears.
<<close_dialogue_bubble>>
<<move_character_keep_facing "Anin" -8.3 2 "walk">>
<<delay 0.5>>
<<start_flinch_character "Anin">>
// Anin: *flinches
Anin: I'm... scared to move on with my life.
Anin: I want to go back...
Anin: Go back and rewind the time I have with my friends.
Anin: I don't want to lose them.
Anin: And I don't want to lose my future, either.

// Revisit the real December 9 Classroom. Its existing Lila speaks the memory.
<<fade_black_out>>
<<memory_montage true>>
<<set $dec10_wish_flashback to true>>
<<replay_cutscene "Dec9_Classroom_Arrival">>
<<set $chapter_scene to 9>>
<<set_time_of_day "morning">>
<<scene_transition_at_x "Classroom" 7.29 "right">>
===

title: Dec10_Wish_AfterFlashback
tags: december10 dorm night wish return
---
<<cinematic_start>>
Anin: ...

// Anin approaches the calendar. Tune the X destination to the calendar prop tomorrow.
<<close_dialogue_bubble>>
<<move_character "Anin" 3 3 "walk">>
<<story_splash "calendar_normal">>
Anin: Well... nothing to lose, I guess.
// This plays the existing paper and writing sounds.
<<edit_calendar>>
<<story_splash "calendar_circled">>
Anin: Me? Believing one of Lila's rumors? I must be really desperate, huh?
<<story_splash_end>>

// Anin walks to bed. The existing sleep pose is a placeholder for the eyes-open beat.
<<close_dialogue_bubble>>
// WakeUpPose places the bed art relative to Anin's root X, so stop at the Dorm Player's
// scene X (-3.41), where every morning wake-up starts. Any other X shifts her in the bed.
<<move_character "Anin" -3.41 3 "walk">>
// Change to the bed pose while the screen is fully covered.
<<fade_black_out>>
<<lie_down "Anin">>
<<fade_black_in>>
<<dialogue_speed 18>>
Anin: Thank you...
Anin: And goodbye, everyone...
<<dialogue_speed 0>>
<<cinematic_end>>
// Camera close-up remains a centered calendar still until the camera shot is made.
<<story_splash "calendar_circled">>
<<begin_loop_one>>
===
